<title>FRANCE: French budget deficit 72.4 bln Ffr end-Feb - finmin.</title>
<headline>French budget deficit 72.4 bln Ffr end-Feb - finmin.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French budget deficit at the end of February stood at 72.4 billion francs, the finance ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The figure compared to a deficit of 90 billion at the end of February 1996, it said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following breakdown of budget receipts: (figures in billions, year on year changes in percent, 1997 year forecast):</p>
<p> REVENUES			end Feb 97  Feb 96  pct	 1997</p>
<p> Net tax receipts		 224.3    226.3  -0.9    1,395.3</p>
<p>  of which: -- income tax	66.9     72.7  -8.0	291.8</p>
<p>  -- net company tax	     -0.7	1.0 -170.0     144.8</p>
<p>  -- petrol duties		 21.5     21.2   1.4	151.9</p>
<p>  -- net Value Added Tax	111.2    106.9   4.0	635.2</p>
<p>  -- miscellaneous		 25.4     24.5   3.7	171.6</p>
<p> Non-tax receipts		  17.2     13.8 -24.6	155.1</p>
<p> Local authority, EU charges  -50.7    -43.5  16.6     -253.9</p>
<p> General budget receipts	202.4    206.4  -1.9    1,296.5</p>
<p> SPENDING			end Feb 97  Feb 96  pct</p>
<p> Ordinary civil spending	212.1    208.3   1.8</p>
<p> of which debt		     19.3     28.6 -32.5</p>
<p> Capital civil spending	   9.0     13.2 -31.8</p>
<p> Ordinary military spending    22.5     23.6   4.7</p>
<p> Capital military spending     15.6     21.6 -27.8</p>
<p> TOTAL BUDGET SPENDING	  259.2    266.7  -2.8</p>
<p>BALANCE</p>
<p> Total net spending	     259.2    266.7  -2.8</p>
<p> Total net receipts	     202.4    206.4  -1.9</p>
<p> General budget deficit	 -56.8    -60.3</p>
<p> Special Treasury Accounts    -15.6    -29.7</p>
<p> TOTAL CENTRAL GOVT DEFICIT   -72.4    -90.0</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5542</p>
</text>
